# Branches and pull requests

Several agents work in this repo in parallel. `main` deploys to GitHub Pages
on every push, so it must only change through reviewed pull requests.

## Workflow

1. Start from fresh `main`: `git fetch origin main && git checkout -b <type>/<short-name> origin/main`
   (`feat/`, `fix/`, `art/`, `chore/`).
2. Keep the change focused on one task. Do not touch gameplay, balance, texts
   or art outside that task.
3. Before pushing, run and make green:
   - `npm run typecheck`
   - `npm run build` (no errors or warnings)
   - for UI/art changes, look at a screenshot (see `scripts/capture-*.mjs`).
4. Push the branch (`git push -u origin <branch>`) and open **one PR into `main`**.
   Describe what changed, how you verified it, and anything intentionally left out.
5. **Never push to `main`** (neither `origin` nor `github` remote) and never
   force-push a shared branch. The owner reviews and merges.
6. If `main` moved and the PR conflicts, merge `origin/main` into your branch
   and re-run the checks.

## Avoid collisions between agents

Stay inside your area; touch shared files only when the task requires it:

- Art / rendering: `src/art/*`, `src/render/*`
- A level: its own `src/scenes/<Level>1995.ts` (one agent per level)
- Core / UI / persistence: `src/core/*`, `src/ui/*`, `src/systems/*`, `src/main.ts`

## Compatibility contracts

- Keep the public debug API `window.__novgorod` (`goto*`, `states`, `beer`,
  `captureCanvas`, `resetSave`, …): `scripts/capture-*.mjs` depend on it.
- Keep the shape of `ProgressFlags` (`src/core/StateManager.ts`) and the save
  format version in `src/core/SaveGame.ts`; changing either needs a migration.
- Vite `base` defaults to `/the-game/`; GitHub Actions sets it from the repo name.
